  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Common",
      "description": "This contains the APIs related to the retrieval of information related to the Common namespace within the Data Standards"
    },
    {
      "name": "Banking",
      "description": "This contains the APIs related to the retrieval of information related to the Banking namespace within the Data Standards"
    },
    {
      "name": "Energy",
      "description": "This contains the APIs related to the retrieval of information related to the Energy namespace within the Data Standards"
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "These endpoints relate to authorisation and authentication."
    },
    {
      "name": "Admin",
      "description": "These endpoints are related to the retrieval of information related to admin"
    },
    {
      "name": "Notification",
      "description": "This contains the APIs related to the sending of notification information to the Data Holder"
    },
    {
      "name": "Device",
      "description": "This contains the APIs related to the retrieval of information related to devices"
    },
    {
      "name": "v1.22.0.0",
      "description": "Uplifts the Data Adapter to be aligned with the Consumer Data Standards 1.22.0.\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n- Changes to `GET /energy/{principalId}/invoice` endpoint:\n  - The description of `accountCharges` field in `EnergyInvoice` is updated to clarify that it is for account level charges and credits.\n- Changes to `userId`, `principalId` and `accountId`:\n  - The maximum length of these fields is now included to document the existing limitations of our database storage. \n"
    },
    {
      "name": "v1.20.0.0",
      "description": "Uplifts the Data Adapter to be aligned with the Consumer Data Standards 1.20.0 and incrementally improves various components.\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n- Changes to `GET /energy/{principalId}/invoice` endpoint:\n  - Clarified that `oldest-date` and `newest-date` query parameters should be used to filter invoice records by invoice issue date\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "v1.19.0.0",
      "description": "Uplifts the Data Adapter to be aligned with the Consumer Data Standards 1.19.0 and incrementally improves various components.\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n- Changes to `GET /energy/{principalId}/account` endpoint according to [Decision Proposal 260](https://github.com/ConsumerDataStandardsAustralia/standards/issues/260):\n  - Introduced `status` query parameter in `GET /energy/{principalId}/account` endpoint\n  - Updated `creationDate`, `planOverview` and `planDetail` fields in `AdapterEnergyAccountDetailV1` from required to conditional\n- Changes to `POST /login/user` endpoint:\n  - Introduced `AdapterUserV4`\n  - `principalName` field in `AdapterUserV4` is a required field\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "v1.18.0.0",
      "description": "Uplifts the Data Adapter to be aligned with the Consumer Data Standards 1.18.0 and incrementally improves various components.\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n- Significant alignment to upstream Standards for 1.18.0 particularly regarding descriptions\n- Alignment of `x-cds-type` coupled with internal linting and examples\n- Introduction of 451 Legal Reasons responses to:\n  - `POST /login/verify`\n  - `POST /user/attribute`\n  - `POST /user/principal`\n- Update error responses for HTTP Status 400 to:\n  - `GET /energy/{principalId}/account/{accountId}/payment-schedule`\n  - `GET /energy/{principalId}/account/{accountId}/concession`\n  - `GET /energy/{principalId}/balance`\n  - `GET /energy/{principalId}/invoice`\n  - `GET /energy/{principalId}/billing`\n- Introduce HTTP Status 422 Invalid Page errors to:\n  - `GET /energy/{principalId}/invoice`\n  - `GET /energy/{principalId}/billing`\n- Introduce `customerUType` into response for `POST /login/user` and introduce `AdapterUserV3`\n- Maintenance Iteration 11 changes:\n  - Updated Energy Plan Contract Pricing to include `FLEXIBLE_CONT_LOAD` and `QUOTA` models\n  - Significant rework of Energy Plan Contract in accordance with upstream changes\n  - Updated Energy Plan Discount Category types\n  - Align multiple `startTime` and `endTime` values with RFC3339 aligned `TimeString` from upstream specifications\n  - Updates to Energy Concessions structure\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "v1.16.0.5",
      "description": "Incorporate changes associated with expanding out Multi Party Account support to include Nominated Representatives. Also includes continued uplift to Energy related endpoints.\n\n## Multi Party & Notifications Support\n\n* Introduction of `NOMINATED_REPRESENTATIVE` enumeration to `EnumAdapterAccountRelationshipTypeV1`\n* Introduction of `userId` to `AdapterAccountCustomerV2`\n* Introduction of `userId` to `AdapterAuthorityToOperateV1`\n* Notification API must be implemented by this time to support Notifications FDO\n\n## Feature Related Changes\n\n* Introduction of _Retrieve FRMP Details_ API to support Energy delivery\n\n## Deprecation Notices\n\n* `principalId` has been replaced by `userId` in `AdapterAccountCustomerV2`\n* `principalId` has been replaced by `userId` in `AdapterAuthorityToOperateV1`\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "v1.16.0.3",
      "description": "Incorporate further changes expected to support Multi Party Account (MPA) and Notifications support within the HaaS environment. While the initial target is focused on the Joint Account obligations [Biza.io](http://biza.io/) has attempted to consider Business Account requirements in this release to minimise further future adapter change.\n\nIn addition, this release introduces initial Energy Sector support to the Data Adapter inline with the upcoming Industry Go-Live of Energy currently intended for November 2022.\n\n## Multi Party & Notifications Support\n\n* Get User API now incorporates:\n  * `principalName` representing the presentation name of a Principal during consent flow\n\n## Feature Related Changes\n\n* Introduction of `Get User Principals` and `Get Username Attributes` to support _Biza Managed Authentication_ mechanism\n* Introduction of initial round of Energy sector endpoints\n\n## General Changes\n\n* `DioPrincipalId` has been removed and replaced with an inline definition\n* `DioRealmName` has been removed and replaced with an inline definition\n* Numerous copy fixes including removal of release references in favour of this documentation\n* Numerous alignments of `x-cds-data-type` and removal of invalid CDS specific data types (eg. `AmountString`) from OpenAPI `format` . Light application of `pattern` regexp where simple regular expressions are available.\n* Numerous fixes for invalid values in `required` list following internal linting added to CI\n* Some operations renamed to be industry specific (eg. `listBankingPayees` and `listBankingPayments`) in order to remove ambiguity across industry\n* Moved unused `Get Closed Principals` call to structurally aligned endpoint path\n- Fix DioTransactionDirectDepositV1 to use a `pattern` not a `format` with the regexp\n* Where appropriate `uuid` format has been provided for identifiers\n\n## Deprecation Notices\n\n* `id` fields have been deprecated in favour of more expressive `objectId` style fields\n* `Get Customer` located at `/banking/customer/{principalId}` has been moved to `/customer/{principalId}` to be consistent across sectors. A retirement date for the original endpoint path has not been specified at this time.\n* `Get User ID` operation has been deprecated in favour of endpoints introduced for Biza Managed authentication\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "v1.16.0.0",
      "description": "Incorporates changes expected to support Multi Party Account (MPA) and Notifications support within the HaaS environment. While the initial target is focused on the Joint Account obligations Biza.io has attempted to consider Business Account requirements in this release to minimise further future adapter change.\n\nIn order to support multiple modes of operation the HaaS MPA design incorporates the ability to either be the authoritative source of truth or be a supplicant of the Data Adapter for the following key attributes:\n\n  - Sharing Status of a Joint Account (Pre-approval, Non-Disclosure or Pending)\n  - Vulnerability status of an Account Customer or a specific User\n  - Secondary User relationships for a specific Account\n\n## Multi Party & Notifications\n\n* Get User API now incorporates:\n  * `vulnerable` representing customer vulnerable flag\n  * `authorityToOperate` representing an Authority to Operate over specified Principal identifiers\n* List Banking Accounts has had the following attributes added/updated:\n  * `accountCustomers` containing Joint Accounts _must_ be introduced by this time to comply with Joint Accounts FDO incorporating:\n    * `vulnerable` representing customer vulnerable flag if Adapter is authoritative\n    * `relationship` introduced to describe relationship type\n  * `jointAccountSharingStatus` describing the Joint Account Sharing Status\n- New Notification API introduced to facilitate communication by Holders via preferred channels\n- `extendedDescription` within DioTransaction is required (as per upstream) but was not marked as required in the adapter. \n  Until July 2022, HaaS will default to \"Not Available\" if it encounters this missing required field in existing implementations.\n\n## Payload Related Changes\n- Uplift to Get Payee and Get Payee Detail V2 with the following attributes updated/added:\n  - `digitalWallet` object structure for Digital Wallet payees\n  - Update the `payeeType` to include `DIGITAL_WALLET`\n\n## Feature Related Changes\n- Introduction of Get Health endpoint to allow for live health checks\n- Introduction of `x-haas-realm-name` header to communicate the active realm being processed\n- Introduce Token Based Authentication as an alternative to API-Key based authentication\n\n## General Changes\n- Model naming structure has been altered to avoid namespace collision and in preparation for Energy introduction\n- Fixed required list in Account schema that specified a non existent field of `productId`\n- `physicalAddresses` within `AdapterOrganisationV2` (fka `DioOrganisationV1`) and `DioPersonV1` has had clarifying statements added inline with Standards updates - zero valid physical addresses is now considered a compliant response\n- Numerous copy fixes\n\n## Deprecation Notices\n- `customerId` has been replaced by `principalId` value from `AdapterAccountCustomerV2` (fka `DioAccountCustomerV1`)\n- `owner` has been deprecated in favour of `relationship` in `AdapterAccountCustomerV2` (fka `DioAccountCustomerV1`) \n- `agentFirstName`, `agentLastName` and `agentRole` in `AdapterOrganisationV2` (fka `DioOrganisationV1`) as they are intended to be superseded by Multi Party Account support\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "v1.11.0.0",
      "description": "## Payload Related Changes\n- Introduction of payeeReference and nickname into BankingScheduledPaymentToV1\n- Introduction of Enhanced Error Handling compatible error codes\n  - NOTE: Existing error responses and behaviours will remain until Enhanced Error Handling uplift is activated\n- Introduction/Alignment of IneligibleBlock and LegalBlock error responses\n- Introduction of text transaction filter into Get Transactions call\n\n## General Changes\n- Alignment to 4 digit x.y.z.a format aligned with DSB 1.11.0\n- Alignment of Adapter specific errors to CDR Standards format\n- Reset of tag names to generalised names\n- Ensure requestId is mandatory in login verify\n- Make APIKey generic in line with configurability of header name\n- Dropping of DioErrorV1, BadRequest models as they are superseded by more explicit response type definitions\n- Numerous copy fixes\n\n## Deprecation Notices\n- loginId have been replaced by username and support for it will be dropped in future releases\n- ErrorInvalidUsernameV1 represents an undocumented but currently supported method of rejecting OTP initiation at Step 1.\n  Due to potential for enumeration attack exposure this has never been recommended and is immediately scheduled for deprecation.\n- crnType was dropped in Standards 1.7.0 and is no longer required\n\n"
    }
  ],
